Implement the recorded design so the agreed requirements are met. Stay inside the declared write scope. Do not create commits and do not run repository commands: the controller owns verification and Git.

{{outputs.featureDesign}}

{{outputs.featureRequirements}}

Review the Worker's change against the recorded requirements and design. State which acceptance criteria the repository now satisfies and which it does not. Judge only what the repository shows and what Bachata's own verification reports.

Answer with exactly one JSON object and nothing else. It carries two fields: "candidate", the Candidate fingerprint Bachata gave you, copied exactly; and "review", an object with "verdict" set to either accept or reject, a one-sentence "summary", and "defects", a list. An accept carries an empty defects list. A reject carries between one and ten defects, each with "id", "severity" (blocker, major or minor), "statement", "requiredChange" and "evidence", and each naming a change a Worker can make. Bachata restates the exact shape in its own review block. Prose is not a verdict and fails the task.

